"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T21:50:43-07:00","id":1257917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1255816-exalted-storytellers-vault-is-now-open?p=1257845#post1257845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I approve new members if they answer the questions, but if not I don\u2019t let them in as we had some spammers and folks who didn\u2019t realize the group was for content creators not general game discussion (there are other groups for that).<br /> <br /> M</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since the first question changed since I applied, I'll assume it was an innocent technical error related to the switchover that stopped you from approving me, and look forward to you approving now that there's an answer to the <i>new</i> first question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T02:17:59-07:00","id":1258162,"title":"","content":"Can you use your own art (or other art you have permission to use) or only that from the packs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T11:50:19-07:00","id":1258238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1255816-exalted-storytellers-vault-is-now-open?p=1258162#post1258162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use your own art (or other art you have permission to use) or only that from the packs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ToS says:<br /> <br /> Art<br /> <br /> No artwork may be used from any White Wolf publications, except those specifically made available here on StorytellersVault.com. You may use artwork from the Storytellers Vault\u2019s art selection and public domain artwork. You must have permission to use any artwork. Please read the FAQ further for more information on the use of art and logos in your content.<br /> <br /> Content creators are required to have secured any image release rights from any models that may appear in any illustrations or photography.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Ok, it also says this:<br /> <br /> For now, we ask that you publish RPG supplements, fiction, illustrations, comics, graphic novels, and photography only, please. <br /> <br /> What kinds of artwork and maps can I use in my Storytellers Vault titles?<br /> <br /> The artwork (such as illustrations or maps) that you include in your title does not become part of the Storytellers Vault content that other Storytellers Vault contributors can then use. Here is general advice for these types of artwork:<br /> <br /> Art and maps provided by White Wolf. The art you find in the Resources for Storytellers Vault category is owned by White Wolf and can be freely used in your Storytellers Vault titles. No other artwork from White Wolf titles can be used \u2014 only the art specifically released in Art Packs for Storytellers Vault Creators. Art released by White Wolf is brand specific and can only be used in association with its specific overarching brand of products. For example; Exalted art packs can only be used for Exalted and World of Darkness art packs can only be used for World of Darkness. However, any art assets can be used across game lines as long as it is within the same larger brand (e.g. Mage can be used for vampire, Werewolf for Changeling etc).<br /> <br /> Public Domain Art. Art that you are certain is in the public domain can be used.<br /> <br /> Stock Art. Usage of stock art depends on the license associated with that stock art. Most of the stock art sold under the Publisher Resources category on DriveThruRPG includes a license that would allow it to be used in your Storytellers Vault titles.<br /> <br /> Commissioned Art. Usage of art that you commission from an artist depends upon your terms with the artist. You must have the rights or license to use the art in your title. The artwork does not become owned by OneBookShelf or by White Wolf; you simply must have rights to use it in your commercial work.<br /> <br /> Creative Commons. This depends on the type of Creative Commons license. Some allow commercial use, others do not.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if you\u2019ve commissioned something, double check with the artist and maybe get them to sign something, but if you made it yourself it looks like you should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 09-30-2018, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T21:05:08-07:00","id":1259176,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason that the Exalted Art Pack #3 didn't include any art from Aspect Book Fire? Might we see that art turn up in a future art pack or have this art pack updated to include it later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T21:08:11-07:00","id":1259177,"title":"","content":"Also, art pack #2 appears to be working now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T22:06:05-07:00","id":1260077,"title":"","content":"Does anyone 